{"additions":11,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTc4OTcy","is_bot":false,"login":"Yudis-bit","name":"Yudistira Putra"},"baseRefName":"master","body":"### Description\n\n`src/ctime_tests.c` currently exercises `secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign32` under Valgrind/CHECKMEM, but does not call the public `secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign_custom` entry point.\n\n`sign_custom` is not only an alias: it accepts optional `extraparams` (including a custom nonce function) and variable message length before calling the shared internal signer. Functional tests cover it, but not under the constant-time CHECKMEM harness.\n\nThis PR adds a minimal direct call to `secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign_custom(..., NULL)` with secret material undefined under CHECKMEM (default nonce path).\n\n### Coverage gap (why)\n\nPlanted local-only synthetic mutations unique to the `sign_custom` entry (secret-dependent branch / secret-dependent static table load that do not change signature output) were **not** detected by the existing ctime suite, but **were** detected after this one-call addition. A constant-work control mutation remained clean.\n\nThis is a **test-coverage** improvement. **No production cryptographic code is modified.** This PR does **not** claim a real production vulnerability in unmodified libsecp256k1.\n\n### Change\n\n- `src/ctime_tests.c` only (+11 lines)\n- No mutation code\n- No new dependencies\n\n### Build / test\n\n```bash\ncmake -B build \\\n  -DSECP256K1_VALGRIND=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_BUILD_CTIME_TESTS=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_SCHNORRSIG=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_EXTRAKEYS=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_ECDH=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_RECOVERY=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_ELLSWIFT=ON \\\n  -DSECP256K1_ENABLE_MODULE_MUSIG=ON\ncmake --build build --target ctime_tests\nvalgrind --error-exitcode=42 ./build/bin/ctime_tests\n```\n\nClean upstream + this test: pass (repeated).  \nSynthetic mutations were local-only and are not included in this branch.\n\n### Limitations\n\n- Default nonce path only; a dedicated custom-nonce callback CHECKMEM case can be a follow-up.","changedFiles":1,"comments":[],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-17T17:27:39Z","authors":[{"email":"85178972+Yudis-bit@users.noreply.github.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTc4OTcy","login":"Yudis-bit","name":"Yudistira Putra"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-17T17:27:39Z","messageBody":"Call secp256k1_schnorrsig_sign_custom with CHECKMEM-undefined secrets\nso the public sign_custom entry point is exercised under Valgrind, not\nonly schnorrsig_sign32.","messageHeadline":"test: cover schnorrsig_sign_custom in constant-time tests","oid":"c64c477b095d9b4c9acdf625875d6f9d81def57e"}],"deletions":0,"headRefName":"yudis/ctime-cover-schnorrsig-sign-custom","headRefOid":"c64c477b095d9b4c9acdf625875d6f9d81def57e","headRepositoryOwner":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTc4OTcy","name":"Yudistira Putra","login":"Yudis-bit"},"isDraft":true,"latestReviews":[],"mergeStateStatus":"UNSTABLE","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","reviewDecision":"","reviewRequests":[],"reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-17T17:28:29Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/actions/runs/29600137887/job/87950067246","name":"Build x64 Docker image","startedAt":"2026-07-17T17:28:15Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-17T17:28:42Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/actions/runs/29600137887/job/87950067240","name":"Build arm64 Docker image","startedAt":"2026-07-17T17:28:18Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-07-17T17:37:57Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/bitcoin-core/secp256k1/actions/runs/29600137887/job/87950067370","name":"x86_64: macOS Sequoia, Valgrind (int64, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes)","startedAt":"2026-07-17T17:30:43Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},